Changes: Android.mk dropped (built by LineageOS kernel.mk).

Xiaomi compatibility (ST54SPI_XIAOMI_COMPAT, set in Kbuild; "XIAOMI-COMPAT"
blocks in st54spi_gpio.c): reference-counted ST54SPI_SET_GPIO power and no
ST54SPI_RESET_GPIO, matching the stock amethyst stm_st54se_gpio.ko.
  No Xiaomi source with this logic is published. The QTI/Xiaomi
  st/opensource/eSE-driver trees checked (xiaomi-8550-kernel/
  android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8550-modules branch uvite, commit
  0cce8308d8c1e1f2eca45fb6dcbfe3c8ade7c008) do not have it. The behaviour
  was written from a specification derived from the stock binary (see
  docs/amethyst-drivers/nfc.md); no decompiled code was used. It adds a
  mutex around the counter, which stock lacks.
